      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carencro%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s culture today traces back to the 1700s and 1800s influx of Acadian and African settlers who built a community rooted in tradition and faith.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://carencro.org/about/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Carencro’s historic Brass Band, founded by a local musician, still plays clarinet melodies that echo the town’s musical heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carencro%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By 1889, Carencro boasted two sugar mills and shipped 1,800 bales of cotton from its station to distant markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carencro%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The modern City Hall and Fire Station complex, crafted by local architect Lynn Guidry, contrasts sharply with the historic Catholic church.",
